  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 303 AM MST WED NOV 18 2026\nA brief upper-level ridge will build in the region behind the upper \nlow on Saturday, providing dry conditions until the next strong low \npressure system begins to move into the northwest coast late \nSaturday/early Sunday. Latest guidance now has the first band of \nprecipitation brought about by this low arriving over eastern OR \nearly Sunday. The precip coverage for Sunday remains weak, with \nunder 30% chances for valleys and up to 50% for mountains. Another \nbrief upper-level ridge will sweep across the area Monday into early \nTuesday before another Pacific system moves in and brings widespread \nprecipitation chances yet again for Wednesday. Temperatures \nwill hover near or slightly below normal in SW Idaho and 5-10 \ndegrees below normal in SE Oregon throughout the long term \nperiod. Breezy winds will accompany systems passing through.",
